comments for API contracts, invariants, sentinel values, and units.
subtractive-engineering.md orders aggressive deletion while simple.md forbids
deleting code you do not understand. Do not "fix" these unprompted; Aaron chose
the tradeoff with the contradictions stated in front of him.

These files were last tuned for Fable 5 in 83a9a71, not for Opus 5. That
staleness was part of a416b36's rationale and it is back. Relevant if prompt
quality problems show up.

## Codebase Discoveries
plugins/abatilo-core/CLAUDE.md carries a MANDATORY version-bump rule, and it is
DIRECTORY-SCOPED, so it only enters context after reading a file inside that
subtree. Two prior notes (1745fbc, 4917a6b) record agents nearly missing it. I
read it explicitly before committing.

Its version table has no row for removing an active skill. Adding a skill is
MINOR and "removal of deprecated code" is PATCH. I treated removing a live
skill as the inverse of adding one and went MINOR.

Nothing outside the deleted files referenced them. reporting.md and the
technical-writing SKILL.md only referenced each other, verified by grep across
*.md and *.json.

